      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "CONTINUES",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Continues employment",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Appointment or engagement under subsection 43(2)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "As an officer or temporary employee of the Corporation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2014c00762-sec-15",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15 Application of moneys",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2014c00762#sec-15"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2014c00762.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2014c00762.pdf, p.7",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Australian Broadcasting Commission is liable to pay any\nremuneration and allowances that become payable under Part III of\nthe Australian Broadcasting Corporation Act 1983 before the\ncommencing day and, notwithstanding section 70 of the\nBroadcasting and Television Act 1942, the moneys of the\nCommission may be applied in payment of any such remuneration\nor allowances.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Australian Broadcasting Commission is liable to pay any\nremuneration and allowances that become payable under Part III of\nthe Australian Broadcasting Corporation Act 1983 before the\ncommencing day and, notwithstanding section 70 of the\nBroadcasting and Television Act 1942, the moneys of the\nCommission may be applied in payment of any such remuneration\nor allowances.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2014c00762-sec-15-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2014c00762-sec-15-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "74b6111dd4461df801ff6325a00e35c4a61260c6126392ab7838d5f817804328",
      "skos:note": "Pay remuneration and allowances before commencing day"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2014c00762#sec-15",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15 Application of moneys",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 7,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Australian Broadcasting Commission is liable to pay any\nremuneration and allowances that become payable under Part III of\nthe Australian Broadcasting Corporation Act 1983 before the\ncommencing day and, notwithstanding section 70 of the\nBroadcasting and Television Act 1942, the moneys of the\nCommission may be applied in payment of any such remuneration\nor allowances."
    },
